SUMMARY:Agent Orchestration in the Enterprise: Coordination\, Control\, an
 d Scale
DESCRIPTION:Data Science Raleigh\nAs enterprises move from isolated AI ass
 istants to interconnected agentic systems\, orchestration is becoming a cr
 itical layer of the AI stack. Coordinating multiple agents across tools\, 
 data sources\, models\, and workflows introduces new opportunities for aut
 omation—but also new challenges around reliability\, governance\, observ
 ability\, and control.\n\nThis session explores what it takes to design an
 d operationalize agent orchestration in enterprise environments. From assi
 gning roles and managing handoffs to monitoring performance and enforcing 
 guardrails\, we’ll examine how organizations can build coordinated agent
  systems that scale without sacrificing trust\, security\, or human oversi
 ght.\n\n**You’ll Learn:**\n\n* From Agents to Systems: How orchestration
  enables multiple agents\, models\, tools\, and workflows to work together
  toward shared business objectives.\n* Coordination and Handoffs: Approach
 es for assigning tasks\, managing dependencies\, resolving conflicts\, and
  maintaining context across agents.\n* Control and Observability: How to m
 onitor agent behavior\, evaluate performance\, and intervene when workflow
 s break down or produce unexpected outcomes.\n* Scaling Responsibly: Strat
 egies for governing\, securing\, and scaling agentic systems while maintai
 ning accountability and appropriate human oversight.\n\n**[Register here](
 https://datasciconnect.com/events/webinars/agent-orchestration-in-the-ente
 rprise-coordination-control-and-scale/)**
